{#
  ============================================================================
  CUSTOMER PROOF SLOT — FAILS SAFE, EMPTY BY DEFAULT
  ============================================================================

  DIWEBA has NO verified customer proof. See CLAUDE.md and spec §1.

  This partial exists so that verified proof can be added later without
  restructuring the page. It currently renders NOTHING — no heading, no
  container, no skeleton, no "coming soon", no hidden element. There is no
  placeholder in the DOM for a crawler, a screen reader or an AI system to find
  and misread as a real claim.

  Hiding an empty section with CSS would still put it in the markup. Emitting
  nothing is the only version that cannot leak.

  TWO GATES BEFORE ANYTHING RENDERS. An entry appears only when BOTH are true:

      verified_by_client  — the client has confirmed the facts are accurate
      consent_on_file     — written permission to publish their name/logo exists

  Both default to false. Publishing unverified proof therefore requires two
  deliberate acts, neither of which can happen by accident.

  *** PROHIBITED FOREVER ***
  The "Schreinerei Baumann" material in DIWEBA/diweba-copy.js and the contract
  templates under DIWEBA/ is DEMO DATA from a proposal template, not a real
  customer. Its supporting documents carry placeholder legal text, a dummy SEPA
  creditor ID and a fake tax number. It must never appear on this website as a
  testimonial, case study, metric, review or client reference.

  Never generate an example to "show how it would look". If proof is requested
  and none exists, say so.
#}
{%- set verified = [] -%}
{%- for item in (caseStudies or []) -%}
  {%- if item.verified_by_client and item.consent_on_file -%}
    {%- set verified = (verified.push(item), verified) -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}

{%- if verified.length %}
<section class="proof" aria-labelledby="proof-heading">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 id="proof-heading" class="proof__heading">{{ proofHeading }}</h2>
    <ul class="proof__list">
      {%- for item in verified %}
      <li class="proof__item">
        <blockquote class="proof__quote">
          <p>{{ item.quote[lang] }}</p>
          <footer class="proof__attribution">
            <cite>{{ item.attribution }}</cite>
            {%- if item.client %}<span class="proof__client">{{ item.client }}</span>{% endif %}
          </footer>
        </blockquote>
      </li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
{%- endif %}
